<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     DAYLIGHT SAVING TRANSITION INFOGRAPHIC & EXPLANATION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="content-section" id="dst-explained">
  <h2>Hawaii's Non-DST Policy vs US East Coast DST Shifts</h2>
  <p>
    Unlike most US states, Hawaii has opted out of Daylight Saving Time under the Uniform Time Act of 1966. This leads to seasonal adjustments when calculating HST to EST/EDT:
  </p>

  <!-- SVG DST Diagram -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 750px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="700" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      
      <g transform="translate(30, 40)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="35" rx="6" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" />
        <text x="15" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#f4fbff">Winter (November – March):</text>
        <text x="230" y="22" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#36c7b5">HST (UTC-10) vs EST (UTC-5)</text>
        <text x="540" y="22" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#8fd7ff">+5 Hours EST</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(30, 100)">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="40" rx="6" fill="#1b536e" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="15" y="25" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5">Summer (March – November):</text>
        <text x="230" y="25" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#f4fbff">HST (UTC-10) vs EDT (UTC-4)</text>
        <text x="540" y="25" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#36c7b5">+6 Hours EDT</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <p>
    During winter (November through March), add 5 hours to HST to find EST. During summer (March through November), add 6 hours to HST to find EDT.
  </p>
</section>

